Let him be strong … Taz: Matter and form struggle; soul must dominate matter—“evil inclination from youth”—daily battle; Isaiah 31 “from their roaring …”; Shmuel I 2:9—Samuel I [there] “He guards His pious ones’ footsteps … wicked stumble in darkness.” Rema concludes “not by might”—needs Heaven’s help—human initiates … Iyov … Job … Midrash Tehillim: “there is Tehillim showing …” Yetzer stronger than man—“who can argue with stronger”—person must be bold in mind—therefore “lion”—lion fears no shepherd though men stronger—person strengthens boldly; difficulty “bold as leopard” before mockers less heroic—thinks them peers—but against angelic strong inclination called gibbor—“who is gibbor”—Rema resolved well first two [paragraphs] positive commandments last two negative—see there.
